CoreGS
======

CoreGS is a hardware-faithful PlayStation 2 Graphics Synthesizer renderer for Vulkan,
released under the MIT licence (see LICENSE).

Origin
------

CoreGS was extracted from GT4Recomp (https://github.com/moesuito/gt4-staticrecomp), an MIT
static recompilation of Gran Turismo 4, at commit ebfe1ca5 (branch release/1.3.0-rc15,
2026-11-06). The renderer there is called CoreGS 2.0 and was written from GT4Recomp's own
clean-room specification of the PS2 GS hardware. This repository keeps that code, removes
the Gran Turismo 4 content rules from the generic core (they now live in profiles/gt4 as an
example) and publishes the renderer on its own.

No game data, no disc image, no BIOS, no save, no capture and no game executable is part of
this repository.

Clean room
----------

CoreGS is a clean-room implementation: it was written from the PS2 hardware documentation and
from observing the GS register and packet interfaces, not from the source of another emulator
or renderer. No GPL code and no code or text derived from another emulator is included. See
CONTRIBUTING.md for the rule contributors must follow.

Third-party components
----------------------

- src/replace/third_party/stb_image.h: stb_image by Sean Barrett and contributors, MIT licence
  (or public domain, at your option). Used to load texture-replacement PNGs.
- src/replace/third_party/xxhash.h: xxHash by Yann Collet, BSD 2-Clause licence. Used for the
  texture-replacement pack checksums.

Both files keep their own copyright headers. They are the only third-party code in the
repository; everything else is MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 João Alano and GT4Recomp contributors.
